JisoCreator Installation Guide
==============================

This guide explains how to build, install, and run JisoCreator from source or
from the generated distribution package.


1) Requirements
---------------

- Java JDK 21 or newer
- Maven 3.6 or newer
- Git

ISO creation backend:
- Linux: `mkisofs` must be installed and available in the configured path.
  Default expected path: `/usr/bin/mkisofs`
- Windows: the project package already includes `mkisofs.exe` under
  `res/mkisofs/`


2) Get the source code
----------------------

From GitHub:

    git clone https://github.com/Cavallinux/jisocreator.git
    cd jisocreator

Windows PowerShell equivalent:

    git clone https://github.com/Cavallinux/jisocreator.git
    Set-Location .\jisocreator


3) Build the application
------------------------

Linux build (default profile):

    mvn clean package

Windows build (from any OS, for packaging with Windows SWT artifacts):

    mvn clean package -Pwindows

Optional CLI smoke build profiles:

    mvn clean package exec:exec -Plinux-cmdlinemode
    mvn clean package exec:exec -Pwindows-cmdlinemode

Build output:
- Main runnable jar: `target/jisocreator.jar`
- Distribution zip:
  - Linux: `target/jisocreator-<version>-gtk.linux.x86_64.zip`
  - Windows: `target/jisocreator-<version>-win32.win32.x86_64.zip`


4) Install from generated distribution zip (recommended)
--------------------------------------------------------

4.1 Linux

1. Build with `mvn clean package`
2. Extract `target/jisocreator-<version>-gtk.linux.x86_64.zip`
3. Move extracted files to your install directory (for example `/opt/jisocreator`)
4. Make launcher executable:

       chmod +x /opt/jisocreator/jisocreator.sh

5. Run:

       cd /opt/jisocreator
       ./jisocreator.sh

4.2 Windows

1. Build with `mvn clean package -Pwindows`
2. Extract `target/jisocreator-<version>-win32.win32.x86_64.zip`
3. Open a terminal in the extracted directory
4. Run:

       jisocreator.bat


5) Run directly from build output (without zip install)
-------------------------------------------------------

After `mvn clean package`:

    java --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -jar target/jisocreator.jar

With debug port (5005), Linux/macOS shell style:

    java -agentlib:jdwp=transport=dt_socket,server=y,suspend=n,address=*:5005 \
         --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED \
         -jar target/jisocreator.jar

With debug port (5005), Windows PowerShell style:

    java -agentlib:jdwp=transport=dt_socket,server=y,suspend=n,address=*:5005 --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -jar .\target\jisocreator.jar


6) First-run configuration
--------------------------

On first run, JisoCreator creates user configuration under:

    ~/.config/jisocreator/

If needed, edit:

    ~/.config/jisocreator/jisocreator.properties

Important property:
- `mkisofs.path` (must point to a valid mkisofs executable)


7) Verify installation
----------------------

Run:

    java --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -jar target/jisocreator.jar --version

You can also validate CLI help:

    java --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -jar target/jisocreator.jar --help

If you built with the Windows profile and are testing from PowerShell:

    java --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -jar .\target\jisocreator.jar --version
    java --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -jar .\target\jisocreator.jar --help


8) Optional: customize log directory
------------------------------------

Default log directory is `./logs`.

Custom path:

    java -Dpath.logs=/custom/log/path --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED \
         -jar target/jisocreator.jar
